IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa6-dual-capacity.l4: the Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 12 (Company secretaries), the cross-heading "Person
-- acting in dual capacity": s 280 (lines 3714-3716 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). Layer 1 of the part agent coa6.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER: as in coa6-private-and-public.l4. s 280 is a flat negative ("is not satisfied"), so where its three
-- conditions all hold the answer is JUST FALSE; outside its scope (it speaks of a provision that asks for BOTH a director AND the
-- secretary, done by or to the SAME person in both capacities) the answer is NOTHING, and a caller must never turn that into TRUE
-- or into FALSE.

§ `Part 12 -- Company secretaries`

§§ `Person acting in dual capacity`

-- ---- s 280: Acts done by person in dual capacity -----------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:3716 | A provision requiring or authorising a thing to be done by or to a director and the secretary of a company is not satisfied by its being done by or to the same person acting both as director and as, or in place of, the secretary.
@ref s 280 Acts done by person in dual capacity (src:3716)
GIVEN `the provision requires or authorises a thing to be done by or to a director and the secretary of a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing is done by or to the same person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that person acts both as director and as, or in place of, the secretary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 280 the provision is satisfied by the thing being done by or to the one person` MEANS
    IF       `the provision requires or authorises a thing to be done by or to a director and the secretary of a company`
         AND `the thing is done by or to the same person`
         AND `that person acts both as director and as, or in place of, the secretary`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not satisfied by its being done by or to the same person acting both as director and as, or in place of, the secretary"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A provision requiring or authorising a thing to be done by or to a director and the secretary of a company"
